<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12559"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:kathiemoffett@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Dahlia<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dahlia<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 10:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7356953.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7356953.html</a> <BR> <BR>Interesting. I&#39;m looking forward to part 2, which I guess is where she&#39;ll get into the bit about his drugging her.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12559-->
<!--Post: 12562--><!--Time: 1112425233-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 11:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My question is...if she suspected Denny of poisoning her, how did she think he was doing it? Surely she wasn&#39;t drinking from the pot of coffee he made. Maybe he used a tranquilyzer gun.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12562-->
<!--Post: 12563--><!--Time: 1112425727-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12563"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 11:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another question...did it never occur to her, at least after March 2004, that someone who was controlling, the correct age, matched the general description, wore a brown uniform, apparently hated women, liked killing animals, surely wrote memos in &#34;that BTK way&#34; and that she had every reason in the world to think was some evil whacko might just possibly be BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12563-->
<!--Post: 12604--><!--Time: 1112546643-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12604"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 03, 2005 - 9:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since the apparent mod of death often blinds police and medical examiners, it would be interesting to see if they ran a tox screen on the Oteros. I doubt it because of the sophistication of equipment and lack of knowledge as to what to look for. Since many vet medications were available then, Jerkface may have used a &#39;hot shot&#39; to subdue the adult Oteros at least. That would explain his ability to gain control over 4 people trained in the martial arts. Did the ME search for puncture marks? It would be helpful to have the autopsy reports made public. With olive skinned persons, the needle sites would not be as readily visible. And I do not believe that Joe and Julie died without a fight for their lives and the lives of their children.  <BR> <BR>The State of Kansas needs to go over every homicide they have with a superfine toothed comb and put this piece of sh&#42;&#42; to death. I do believe that would be an easier resolution for his family than keeping him alive for the rest of his life. If Kansas prisons are anything like those in Texas, he won&#39;t survive very long in the general population. Child killers do not fare well amongst the other prisoners. And he will kill again if he is released through some loophole. Never say never or always.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12604-->
<!--Post: 12618--><!--Time: 1112586264-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12618"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 03, 2005 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Beattie&#39;s book has a &#34;version&#34; of the autopsies performed on the Oteros &#40;I don&#39;t know how comprehensive they are&#41;. It does say that they could find traces of alcohol in Joe SR.&#39;s blood and mentioned negetive results for barbituates and some other drugs, but it doesn&#39;t mention if they were tested for doggie downers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12618-->
<!--Post: 12638--><!--Time: 1112652137-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12638"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 3:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, <BR> <BR>It never would matter if Rader killed kids or not. His high profile status makes him a target for many prison executioners looking for notoriety and to &#34;go down in history.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Unlike Dahmer&#39;s murderer who has gotten little publicity, imo the guy that shanks Rader will be a hero.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12638-->
<!--Post: 12639--><!--Time: 1112654154-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12639"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now remember that Dennis did not work as a compliance officer/dog catcher back when the Oteros were murdered.  In fact it doesn&#39;t look like he had a job at all during that time.  He&#39;d been laid off from Coleman&#39;s a few months earlier and he had not yet begun working for ADT.  I think that was not until November of 1974.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12639-->
<!--Post: 12644--><!--Time: 1112664015-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12644"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 6:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There appears to be many gaps in the employment history of Dennis Rader. <BR>He returns to Wichita sometime in 1970 but isn&#39;t employed at Leeker&#39;s IGA until 1971. He dosn&#39;t start work at Coleman until June of 1972 so there may have been some unemployment between the IGA and Colemans. After leaving Colemans in July of 1973 he appaers to unemployed until November of 1974. He now works his longest continuous job at ADT from November 1974 until July of 1988. 14 years. He then seems to be unemployed again from July 1988 until January 1990 when he becomes Census supervisor for the Wichita area. Then comes another unemployment gap from January 1991 to May of 1991 when he begans his next nearly 14 years of continuous employment as a Park city Compliance Officer.  <BR>I know he was also going to college in the 1970&#39;s but he was married with kids so he still had to work. The unemployment gaps are frequent and sometimes lengthy.  <BR>I wonder if he may have worked spot jobs for &#39;under the table&#39; cash like many people did and do. He may have had a history as a steady worker who when not having a steady job and going to school and collecting unemployment is out looking for a series of under-the-table-pay-part-time jobs. This could explain odd hours away from home that didn&#39;t draw suspicion from his wife and family members. It could also explain the word Handyman in one of his communication codes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12644-->
<!--Post: 12646--><!--Time: 1112674156-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12646"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 04, 2005 - 9:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good thinking, Johno.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12646-->
<!--Post: 12661--><!--Time: 1112710278-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 7:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Couple of notes, Marnie and a few others were killed during Rader&#39;s &#34;off Work&#34; dates, Since Dee and Marnie both ate in the same Restaurant right before they died, possible Rader worked there. Also other vics. found on the same area to Park City, he wa going to night school and in bars/strip clubs...Also if he wanted to hurt this woman he could used any OTC or street drug or drug perscribed to him etc. She need to have her hair tested to see what, if any narcotic was used.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12661-->
<!--Post: 12662--><!--Time: 1112710584-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12662"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 7:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, its my bet that during one of his lapses from employment, he was working with his plumber brother. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12662-->
<!--Post: 12678--><!--Time: 1112750118-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12678"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 05, 2005 - 6:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s a link to part 2 of this story:  <a href="http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7393064.html" target=_top>http://www.ksn.com/news/stories/7393064.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12678-->
<!--Post: 12694--><!--Time: 1112832623-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12694"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 06, 2005 - 5:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->She never does say HOW Rader managed to administer the &#34;poison&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12694-->
<!--Post: 12702--><!--Time: 1112875610-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12702"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 5:06 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe he pee-ed in her coffee?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12702-->
<!--Post: 12703--><!--Time: 1112877147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12703"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 5:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That was a waste of ink. &#40;cyber ink i guess&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12703-->
<!--Post: 12710--><!--Time: 1112887369-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12710"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t know...I found her unconvincing, and wondered if there wasn&#39;t some drama queeniness going on. Which is not to say that Rader wasn&#39;t likely just as big an ass as she said - I&#39;m certain she was telling the truth there.  <BR> <BR>But poisoning someone is far, far too subtle for him. He was a &#34;classic&#34; serial killer in that the closest he came to pooping where he ate - killing in a zone that could cast suspicion on him - was Marine Hedge, who lived on 6254 Independence, whereas he lived on 6220. I&#39;m sure he was hateful and she may have room for a lawsuit against Park City just for having to put up with him and for their grievance policies, which sound ridiculous, &#40;you have to submit the grievance to the person you have it against? That&#39;s nuts&#41;, but I think the &#34;tranquilizer&#34; thing is part of a certain amount of hypochondria and attention seeking. The stories of captured serial killers are full of people around them who see an opportunity for some desperately needed attention.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12710-->
<!--Post: 12712--><!--Time: 1112888154-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12712"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sidewalker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sidewalker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 8:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was reading an article in the Eagle, that I had not read before. Its regarding how folks viewed Rader, their experiences&#40;Good ones and bad ones&#41; <BR>One woman&#39;s experience is just scary as hell. <BR>Here is a link to the article in case you have not read it either. The woman&#39;s name is Misty King. <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/11062626.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/11062626.htm</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
