<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12720"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 07, 2005 - 7:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think that city officials should severely be taken to task. One does not dismiss consistent conplaints about an employee from so many different people. It would be different if there was one crackpot continually complaining. I think that they were negligent in their official duties to the point of loss of property and life. What a red flag they had and they chose to ignore it. I wonder what else they have swept under their rug.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
