<!--Post: 12742--><!--Time: 1112981129-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12742"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 08, 2005 - 10:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I spoke with my microbiologist/medical lab resource. The substance that is used to paralyze animals is curare: what pygmies put on the end of their darts to stop their prey. It is used in surgeries today to control muscle spasms, etc. It was obtained from the skins of frogs. I should have asked him about oral ingestion. I asked about exhuming someone who had been buried for 30 years. He said that the substance would have to be in significantly large quantities to be id&#39;d after that amount of time. Some things get by the stomach acids and some don&#39;t. Anything mixed with DMSO will go right into the bloodstream. He probably laced her coffee cup/glass with something. Small doses of fungicide, insecticide, herbicide, etc., would make someone sick. Did he go into the ladies&#39; room and taint the toilet paper? Sodium morphate on a toilet seat will untraceably kill, making it appear that one died while having a BM. Rattlesnake venom can be consumed orally with no untoward effects, but mix it with DMSO, apply to the skin, and watch what happens. &#40;I have grilled physicians for years as I read about different deaths.&#41; Hopefully, the police itemized everything that they found in his truck and shed and home, including chemicals. One would get an odd grouping of symptoms when ingesting ag substances. What about animal worming meds, etc.? One woman slowly poisoned her husband with something that was used for aquarium maintenance. One of my physician&#39;s stated that one of his patients was poisoned by her husband. It was a slow process. They knew what he was doing. He spent long amounts of time in the jungles of South America with the natives. The doctor stated that even if they knew what substance was being used, the issue would be developing a blood test to identify it.  She died.  <BR> <BR>I read on another BTK site that it was thought that all blood types degraded to Type O after 24 hours. My source said that is patently not true. A leopard does not change its spots. Both sexes can be secreters and nonsecreters. Well, that is it for now.....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12742-->
<!--Post: 12745--><!--Time: 1112982146-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12745"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 08, 2005 - 10:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey guys - I thought she had already filed a civil lawsuit against him and the city. It would be in the US District Court. I also read, that she had already filed the complaint with the EEOC and they had issued her a right to sue.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12745-->
<!--Post: 12780--><!--Time: 1113186041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12780"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, April 10, 2005 - 7:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t agree with you Steve:I found her unconvincing, and wondered if there wasn&#39;t some drama queeniness going on.  <BR> <BR>Most attorney&#39;s, when weighing this type of potential new client/case &#40;ie. employment law&#41;, will go to great lengths to substantiate allegations before they will instruct and or advise to file an EEOC claim. If the rule is still the same in Kansas, her attorney will not be able to assist her at any hearing the EEOC may have to investigate her allegations. At this point she is on her own. <BR> <BR>And if she was a lil queeny, she wouldn&#39;t have much of a claim anyway. No, there&#39;s no doubt that Rader was a walking prick of a boss, but why did she tolerate it for 6 years? <BR> <BR>If my recall is correct, the Capps family were involved in law enforcment at sometime. If it&#39;s not her exhusband, it could be her brotherinlaw but one of them served on the Park City Police force and ultimately as the Polic Chief.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12780-->
<!--Post: 12787--><!--Time: 1113222781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12787"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 5:33 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky, <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know if this is true or not, but on the kansas.com message board, a poster claims that both her &#40;Mary Capps&#41; brother and her father were on the Park City police force.  In fact, it claims that her father would have been chief of plice at the time she was hired.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12787-->
<!--Post: 12808--><!--Time: 1113281109-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12808"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Women tolerate things for years and years. They allow a pile of crap to accumulate before something rises up inside them and says &#39;this is enough&#39;. Perhaps she thought that things would get better. Since she saw 2 sides to him, perhaps she thought that the good side would eventually come forth. Their complaint system was ridiculous to begin with. Perhaps she wanted to make it on her own, and ride out the storm, so to speak. Women are bad about giving someone the benefit of  the doubt, thinking that they must be misinterpreting the situation or blaming themselves. Female psychology. I am guilty of it. A woman will wait till hell freezes over before taking action on something. Then the dam bursts, and years of stuff comes pouring forth. It could be that they don&#39;t want to be labeled a complainer, or they think that they will not be taken seriously. That is why women &#39;snap&#39; and seem to over react to a situation, when in fact thay are reacting to years and years of crap. Why did she just keep stabbing? Why did she keep driving over the creep? The straw that broke the camel&#39;s back.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12808-->
<!--Post: 12817--><!--Time: 1113290498-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12817"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 12:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I still think that Denny did about everything short of hanging a sign around his neck saying &#34; I AM THE ONE AND ONLY BTK...ARREST ME!&#34; <BR> <BR>Sure there were some people who thought he was the salt of the earth. They seem to be a little suspicious too. Park City may be &#34;almost in Wichita&#34;, but it still seems to have a small town mentality, meaning that everyone knew what everyone was up to &#40;just read the Ark Valley News police report&#41;. <BR> <BR>There is no way that Rader was able to be a Boy Scout, a Party Boy, a Philanderer, a Good Husband And Father, a Fascist, a Choir Boy and a Serial Killer, all at the same time, in a town that size, and no one was the wiser.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12817-->
<!--Post: 12819--><!--Time: 1113291243-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 12:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here&#39;s an interesting tidbit that makes me pause to re-evalutate the apparent &#34;woo-woo&#34; factor on this lady. <BR> <BR>I was just reminded by this Bookworm post &#40;<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/8/14.html#POST12790" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/8/14.html# POST12790</a>&#41; over in Possible Victims about a drug called succinylcholine &#40;often as the chloride salt&#41;, which was apparently used by some murderer to poison some folks. <BR> <BR>It caught my eye when I recalled that &#40;in the days of my youth&#41; this drug was routinely used to euthanize dogs and cats.  Interestingly, this same drug is apparently now considered to be inhumane, along with quite a few other old-timey methods &#40;see: <a href="http://www.nmanimalcontrol.com/euthanasia/HEPP/FAQ.html" target=_top>http://www.nmanimalcontrol.com/euthanasia/HEPP/FAQ .html</a>&#41;.   I suspect that the paralytic aspects and side-effect spectrum are thought to make it inferior.  A quick Google yields a plethora of nasty side-effects that match the kind of diffuse symptoms common among malingerers and hypochondriacs.  I guess it wouldn&#39;t surprise me if Denny was aware of this, and had squirreled some away for his own private pleasure.  The idea that he would take delight in tormenting a female complaint-lodger with it isn&#39;t terribly far-fetched.  True, he&#39;s not a poisoner, and I doubt he would want to kill somebody with it &#40;tox is just too obvious and too easy to get caught&#41;.  It&#39;s also an i.v. drug - I don&#39;t even know if it has any oral activity.  But if it does.... <BR> <BR>BTK &#34;Master&#34;-Card.... <BR> <BR>Old bottle of succinylcholine chloride: $24.95 <BR>Plastic syringe: $1.99 <BR>Office coffee: don&#39;t ask <BR>&#34;Look, Mary!  It&#39;s the Goodyear Blimp!&#34;: free <BR> <BR>Watching a superior female underling with real cop connections suffer: priceless to BTK. <BR> <BR>Ironically, BTK could have noticed this drug mentioned while he was ego-surfing - check out this link on Genene Jones at crimelibrary! - <a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/notorious_murders/angels/genene_jones/6.html?sect=9" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/notorious_murders/ange ls/genene_jones/6.html?sect=9</a> <BR> <BR>Of course, there are some inconsistencies.  The drug is normally given i.v., or i.m. at worst, and I can&#39;t find any oral data for the life of me.  While it might be devoid of activity orally, it could also be sufficiently active to have some effects, but sufficiently diminished to avoid the kinds of serious problems that would have landed Denny in jail much earlier.  Interesting to speculate.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12819-->
<!--Post: 12823--><!--Time: 1113317025-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 7:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tulip - I talked to my Dad and he confirmed what I thought with regards to her family being involved in law enforcement. Now, I&#39;m wondering why she didn&#39;t use the fact that she had LE as family as leverage with Rader. It could be that her family being involved with LE, was Rader&#39;s motivation. In fact as resentful as this prick was, I&#39;d put money on that. <BR> <BR>Teardrop - Your right! Unforunately, many of us do tolerate a lot of crap from male co-workers and bosses. I quess since I work in a firm that brings sexual harassment cases, wrongful termination etc. I figured out a long time ago, I don&#39;t have to tolerate that type of crap because there are laws that protect me from that abuse. I&#39;d just wish that there were more women like Ms. Capps that had the back bone to bring complaints like that against municipalities and hold them responsible for employing such fat boys. <BR> <BR>On a more sorrowful note, I think it was Ms. Capps newphew or son that committed suicide sometime ago. It was devastating to the whole commnuity.  <BR> <BR>Your right BModule - it is a small community I don&#39;t know how LE could have missed DTDC either. His behavior  in the work place certainly should have sent signals to someone with half a brain.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12823-->
<!--Post: 12825--><!--Time: 1113325184-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12825"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 12, 2005 - 9:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;On a more sorrowful note, I think it was Ms. Capps newphew or son that committed suicide sometime ago. It was devastating to the whole commnuity.&#34; <BR> <BR>Any deaths of people connected to rader in any way, especially one connected to a person rader had a grudge against, should be looked at. <BR> <BR>&#40;just my opionion&#41; I think dogface wanted to try everything. from strangling, shooting, stabbing,breaking and entering, using fake id&#39;s to get in....to fake suicides, framing others, drowning, starting fires... <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
